<slide>
  section-transition: slide-right
</slide>

<h1>Across languages</h1>

<p>
  The same function in three languages, one section each under this title, sliding in from the left (<c>section-transition: slide-right</c>). The diff can't match different
  grammars, so moving from one to the next is a plain cross-fade.
</p>

<section>
  <h2>TypeScript</h2>
  <code lang=typescript>
    function clamp(x: number, lo: number, hi: number) {
      return Math.min(Math.max(x, lo), hi);
    }
  </code>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Python</h2>
  <code lang=python>
    def clamp(x, lo, hi):
        return min(max(x, lo), hi)
  </code>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Go</h2>
  <code lang=go>
    func Clamp(x, lo, hi int) int {
    	return min(max(x, lo), hi)
    }
  </code>
</section>

<notes>
  Matching needs two trees of the same language. Between languages the old code fades out and the new one fades in.
</notes>
